  "findings": [
    "Native child index zero is the upper-X/upper-Y/upper-Z octant; bits select lower axes, and center-plane ties select the lower child.",
    "Corner keys use floor after adding spacing times 0.01, subtracting the map origin and multiplying by reciprocal spacing, followed by signed 32-bit conversion.",
    "Indexed output-vertex keys truncate Float32 coordinates scaled by 10000 into signed 64-bit integers. The first inserted position is retained; this is not a distance-radius weld.",
    "Leaf edge vertices are allocated in ascending edge order before triangle case emission.",
    "The indexed triangle emitter rejects faces unless the squared length of its Float32-rounded cross product is strictly greater than 2^-23.",
    "Source progression appends absent-distance, zero-direction and clear-boundary slots before advancing each existing corner record.",
    "The mesh preparation helper clears a per-vertex boundary bit before boundary marking. Source-normal preparation remains unresolved."
  ],
